Subject: winealsa: a MIDI input that fails to connect is not left "in use"

When snd_seq_connect_from() failed, midi_in_open() returned
MMSYSERR_NOTENABLED but kept the device's descriptor and its reference on
the sequencer, so the next open of the same input said MMSYSERR_ALLOCATED.
FL Studio retries every input it lists: on a PipeWire system its MIDI
settings showed "PipeWire-System - input" as FAIL, then a stream of "The
MIDI input device is already allocated. It may be in use by another
application." boxes for a device nothing else had open. Undo the open
before returning.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winealsa.drv/alsamidi.c b/dlls/winealsa.drv/alsamidi.c
--- a/dlls/winealsa.drv/alsamidi.c
+++ b/dlls/winealsa.drv/alsamidi.c
@@ -1180,7 +1180,14 @@
     ret = snd_seq_connect_from(midi_seq, port_in, src->addr.client, src->addr.port);
     seq_unlock();
     if (ret < 0)
+    {
+        /* give the device back: it was never opened, and the next try
+         * must not be told it is in use by another application */
+        memset(&src->midiDesc, 0, sizeof(src->midiDesc));
+        src->seq = NULL;
+        seq_close();
         return MMSYSERR_NOTENABLED;
+    }
 
     TRACE("Input port :%d connected %d:%d\n", port_in, src->addr.client, src->addr.port);
 
